---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="An open letter from Justin to the readers of JustinCredibleTech, the long-form companion to @JCredibleTech: consumer tech, AI, cars and EVs, space, science and health."
>
  <div class="container about"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">About</span><h1>An open letter to our readers</h1><p>Why JustinCredibleTech exists, and what you can expect from it.</p></header><article class="prose letter">
    <p class="salutation">Dear reader,</p>
    <p>
      Thanks for stopping by. If you found your way here, there’s a good chance you’re the kind of
      person who sees a headline like “wait, what just shipped?” and wants the rest of the story.
      Same here. That’s exactly why I built this place.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may already know me as
      <a href="https://x.com/JCredibleTech" rel="noopener noreferrer">@JCredibleTech</a>.
      Short posts are great for breaking news, but some stories need room to breathe: the context,
      the timeline, and the honest answer to “why should I care?” This site is where I give them
      that room.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is now the JustinCredible network, eight sections under one roof:
      <a href={withBase("tech/")}>JustinCredible Tech</a> (consumer tech, hardware, software and gadgets),
      <a href={withBase("ai/")}>JustinCredible AI</a> (AI models, tools, companies and research),
      <a href={withBase("auto/")}>JustinCredible Auto</a> (cars, trucks and transportation),
      <a href={withBase("space/")}>JustinCredible Space</a> (rockets, satellites and missions),
      <a href={withBase("ev/")}>JustinCredible EV</a> (electric vehicles, charging and self-driving),
      <a href={withBase("science/")}>JustinCredible Science</a> (discoveries and research in the natural world),
      <a href={withBase("health/")}>JustinCredible Health</a> (medicine, drug approvals, nutrition and health research) and
      <a href={withBase("politics/")}>JustinCredible Politics</a> (policy and government, reported factually and straightforwardly).
      If it’s new, real, and worth your time, I want to explain it clearly.
    </p>
    <p>
      My promise to you is simple. I’ll keep it accurate, keep it fun, and keep it factual. Even in JustinCredible Politics, you get what happened and what each side says, in straightforward terms.
      If something is a rumor, I’ll call it a rumor. If a company publishes a date and a price,
      you’ll get the date and the price, not hype dressed up as news.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you want the quick hits, follow along on
      <a href="https://x.com/JCredibleTech" rel="noopener noreferrer">@JCredibleTech</a>.
      If you want the full story, start with the <a href={withBase("blog/")}>latest posts</a>,
      or grab the <a href={withBase("rss.xml")}>RSS feed</a> and read on your own schedule.
    </p>
    <p>
      However you got here, I’m genuinely glad you did. Thanks for reading, and thanks for being
      curious.
    </p>
    <p class="signature">-Justin</p>
  </article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .about .prose{max-width:700px;margin-top:2rem}
  .letter .salutation{font-weight:600}
  .letter .signature{margin-top:2rem;font-size:1.35rem;font-style:italic;font-weight:600}
</style>
